      "SourceSection": "Problem 5",
      "SourceExcerpt": "Here is a method for solving the equation \\(\\sqrt{5+x}+10=6\\). Does the method produce the correct solution to the equation? Explain how you know.",
      "SourceLessonArtifact": "src/Edulytics.Core/Curriculum/LessonContent/RichV2/us-ccss-hs-alg2-u03-l14.rich-lesson-v2.json",
      "Treatment": "SOURCE_SCOPED_AUTHORING_WITH_TEACHER_REVIEW",
      "TestsExecuted": "NOT_RUN"
    },
    {
      "SourceElementId": "G11-U03-L14-PRACTICE-015",
      "SourceSection": "Problem 5",
      "SourceExcerpt": "\\(\\begin{align} \\sqrt{5+x}+10 &= 6 \\\\ \\sqrt{5+x} &= \\text-4 &\\text{ (after subtracting 10 from each side)} \\\\ 5+x &= 16 &\\text{ (after squaring both sides)} \\\\ x &= 11 \\\\ \\end{align}\\)",
